# Data is reproducible from the API and the archive — except raw/, which is the
# point-in-time record and CANNOT be reconstructed after the fact. If you ever move this
# project, copy data/raw/ManuallyOrLoseIt. It is small (JSON.gz) and it is the evidence
# trail the backtest depends on.
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/external/
data/raw/.cache/

# data/serving/ is deliberately ABSENT from the list above and IS versioned. Do not add it
# for symmetry with its siblings. It is ~120KB of forecasts, the solved squad, the fixture
# grid and the brief — everything the Streamlit app reads — and committing it is what lets
# the app deploy without the archive, the models or a build step. The page never runs the
# pipeline; it reads what `fpl publish` wrote.

# Uncomment to version the point-in-time snapshots alongside the code:
# !data/raw/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
